<h1><a name="_Toc319671830"></a><a name="_Toc319932216"></a><a name="_Toc54074820"></a><a name="Chapter1_14">1.14&nbsp; </a>PRECINCT LISTS—COMPUTER
PRINTOUTS</h1>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><b><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class="tx"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.14.010&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Filing
- amendment.</span></p>

<p class="tx"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.14.020&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Public
inspection of copies.</span></p>

<p class="tx"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.14.030&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Purchase
of copies.</span></p>

<p class="tx"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.14.040&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Copies
of tapes - purchase for use.</span></p>

<p class="tx"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.14.050&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Copies
- purchase price.</span></p>

<p class="tx"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.14.060&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Statement
to accompany copies.</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><b><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.14.010&nbsp;
Filing - amendment.</span></b><span style="font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp; The elections division shall file with the clerk of the
county council sample forms of the computer printouts which shall indicate the
type of information which will be contained on the copies of the computer
printouts of the current precinct lists of registered voters available for
purchase or inspection.&nbsp; The elections division may amend the forms to include
additional information or to delete information by filing additional or
supplemental samples with the clerk of the county council; provided, however,
that additional or supplemental filings shall not be made during the period of
time commencing ninety days prior to an election and terminating on the date of
the election.&nbsp; (Ord. 15971 § 13, 2007:&nbsp; Ord. 1346 § 1, 1972).</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><b><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.14.020&nbsp;
Public inspection of copies.</span></b><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp; Copies of computer
printouts in the form of samples filed with the clerk of the county council may
be inspected by any member of the public at the office of the elections
division under such reasonable rules and regulations as the division may
prescribe.&nbsp; (Ord. 15971 § 14, 2007:&nbsp; Ord. 1346 § 2, 1972).</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><b><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.14.030&nbsp;
Purchase of copies.</span></b><span style="font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp; Copies of the computer printouts in the form of the
samples filed with the clerk of the county council may be purchased by any
registered voter of the state within ten days after a written request is filed
with the elections division.&nbsp; Either paper copies prepared on the copying
machines being currently used by the county or microfilm copies may be
purchased.&nbsp; (Ord. 15971 § 15, 2007:&nbsp; Ord. 1346 § 3, 1972).</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><b><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.14.040&nbsp;
Copies of tapes - purchase for use.</span></b><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp; Any registered voter of
the state within ten days after a written request is filed with the elections
division may purchase the use of copies of the computer magnetic tapes and
format being currently used by the division, which contain the information from
which the lists of current registered voters are compiled, for use in specific
elections under the following rules and regulations:</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; A.&nbsp; Copies of
the tapes may not be obtained until one hundred ninety days prior to the
specific election for which its use is desired.</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; B.&nbsp; All copies
obtained shall be returned within ten days after the election.</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; C.&nbsp; The person
obtaining copies of the tapes shall sign an affidavit stating the name and
address of each person who will have possession of the tapes and the name and
address of each person who will operate the computers on which the tapes will
be used.</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; D.&nbsp; It is
unlawful for anyone to permit a duplicate copy to be made of all or any part of
any computer magnetic tape obtained pursuant to this chapter or to permit the
use of the computer magnetic tapes to improve, amend, supplement or update the
information contained on any other computer magnetic tape.</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; E.&nbsp; When the
computer magnetic tapes obtained pursuant to this chapter are returned, the
person who obtained them shall sign and deliver to the elections division an
affidavit stating:&nbsp; The name and address of each person who had possession of
the computer magnetic tapes, the name and address of each person who operated
the computers on which the computer magnetic tapes were used; a summary of the
information and material which was obtained by using the tapes such as mailing
labels or alphabetical or geographical lists; that duplicate copies of all or
any portion of the tapes were not made; that the tapes were not used to
improve, supplement, amend or update other computer magnetic tapes; and that
all computer print-outs and copies with the exception of mailing labels were
stamped with the statement contained in K.C.C. 1.14.060.P.</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; F.&nbsp; The person
who obtained the tapes shall also obtain and deliver to the elections division
affidavits from each person who had possession of the tapes or who operated
computers on which the tapes were used containing the information required in
subsection E. of this section.&nbsp; (Ord. 15971 § 16, 2007:&nbsp; Ord. 1346 § 4, 1972).</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><b><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;</span></b></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><b><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.14.050&nbsp;
Copies - purchase price.</span></b><span style="font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp; The purchase price of the copies of
the computer tapes and paper and microfilm copies of the computer print‑outs
shall be established by the elections division by filing with the clerk of the
county council prior to each fiscal year a list of the charges which will be
made for furnishing copies of the tapes or the computer print‑outs during
the next fiscal year.&nbsp; The charges shall be determined on the basis of the
amount necessary to reimburse the county its actual costs for furnishing copies
of the requested tapes and computer print‑outs.&nbsp; (Ord. 15971 § 17, 2007:&nbsp;
Ord. 1346 § 5, 1972).</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><b><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.14.060&nbsp;
Statement to accompany copies.</span></b><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp; Each paper copy of a
computer print‑out, the container for each microfilm copy of a computer
print‑out and the container for each copy of the computer magnetic tape
shall be stamped with the following statement in conformance with RCW
29.04.100:</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; "The
information contained herein shall be used only for political purposes.&nbsp; Any
person who uses the information contained herein for commercial purposes shall
be guilty of a felony and shall be punished by imprisonment for not more than
five years or fine of not more than five thousand dollars, or by both such fine
and imprisonment."&nbsp; (Ord. 1346 § 6, 1972).</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc319671831"></a><a name="_Toc319932217"></a><a name="_Toc54074821">1.16&nbsp; REFERENDUM AND INITIATIVE PETITIONS</a></h1>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><b><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class="tx"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.16.005&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; "Alteration"
defined.</span></p>

<p class="tx"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.16.020&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Filing
proposed measure.</span></p>

<p class="tx"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.16.025&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Form
of petitions for ordinances referred to people.</span></p>

<p class="tx"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.16.035&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Form
of petitions for measures for submission to the King County &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; council.</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.16.040&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Verification of
compliance – notice of acceptance or rejection – &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; numbering
– transmittal to department of elections</span><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">.</span></p>

<p class="tx"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.16.050&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Ballot
title – formulation.</span></p>

<p class="tx"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.16.065&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Time
for filing referendum and initiative petitions.</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.16.100&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Filing initiative
or referendums with clerk – review for alterations – &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; rejection
of pages – notice of rejection – completion of review and &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; transmittal
to department of elections – terminal date for verification &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; and
count of names – notice – withdrawal of signatures – filing of &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; additional
pages – verification and count of names – rejections – &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; transmission
of notice of sufficiency or insufficiency.</span></p>

<p class="tx"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.16.110&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Penalties.</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><b><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.16.005&nbsp;
"Alteration" defined.</span></b><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp; For the purposes of this
chapter, unless the context clearly requires otherwise, "alteration"
means any change to the ballot title or text of the measure on a referendum or
initiative petition that occurs between the time the form and language of the
petition are approved by the clerk of the council and the time when signed
petitions are returned to the clerk.&nbsp; Stray marks, scribbles, notes or
highlighting shall not be an "alteration" as long as the ballot title
and text of the measure are legible.&nbsp; (Ord. 18804 § 2, 2018).</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><b><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1.16.020&nbsp;
Filing proposed measure.</span></b></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; A.&nbsp; If any
individual or committee of individuals desires to petition the council to enact
a proposed measure or to order that a referendum of any ordinance passed by the
council be submitted to the electorate, the individual or committee of
individuals shall file in the office of the clerk of the council a printed or
typewritten copy of the proposed petition in the form provided in this chapter,
accompanied by the name, phone number, email address and post office address of
the individual or committee of individuals proposing the measure.</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; B.&nbsp; Petitions
shall be printed on single sheets of white paper of good quality, eight and
one-half inches in width and fourteen inches in length, with a margin of one
and three-quarters inches at the top for binding.&nbsp; The front side of the
petition shall have a minimum font size of eight point font.&nbsp; Each petition
shall contain:</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; 1.&nbsp; Numbered
lines for not more than twenty signatures on each sheet;</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; 2.&nbsp; The
prescribed ballot title or sufficient room for the ballot title to be inserted
if the ballot title has not yet been prepared by the prosecuting attorney;</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; 3.&nbsp; The form
of the petition on each sheet; and</span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; 4.&nbsp; A full,
true and correct copy of the measure being proposed or referred printed on the
reverse side of the petition or on sheets of paper of like size and quality as
the petition, and a web address if one exists to the measure being proposed or
referred in twelve point font at the top of the reverse side of the petition,
firmly fastened to the petition.&nbsp; (</span><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Ord. 18804 § 3, 2018:&nbsp; Ord. 18618 § 14, 2017:&nbsp; <span style="letter-spacing:-.1pt">Ord. 584 § 2, 1970: &nbsp;Ord. 159 § 2, 1969).</span></span></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&quot;Arial&qu[Truncated]